{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2132-12-21 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I’m Dr. Patel, one of your surgical doctors. You’re here today for a skin graft on your right leg wound. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2132-12-21 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’m okay, just a little nervous. The wound’s been slow to heal, and I’m worried it won’t take."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2132-12-21 14:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s completely understandable. We’ve reviewed your history, and because of your diabetes and poor circulation, healing has been tough. But this graft is the next step to help it close properly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2132-12-21 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt? And what exactly are you doing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2132-12-21 14:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll put you to sleep, so you won’t feel anything. First, we’ll clean out any dead tissue—that’s called debridement. Then we’ll take a thin layer of skin from another area and place it over the wound."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2132-12-21 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, so you’re taking skin from somewhere else? Where?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2132-12-21 14:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Usually from your thigh. It’s a split-thickness graft, so it’s very thin and will heal well there. The main goal is to give your leg wound a better chance to heal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2132-12-21 14:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. And after? What happens?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2132-12-21 14:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll go back to your room, on bed rest for a few days. We’ll put a wound vacuum—VAC—on it to help the graft stay in place and prevent infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2132-12-21 14:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that from last time. It helps with healing, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2132-12-21 14:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. It removes fluid and keeps the area clean. You’ll also get antibiotics to prevent infection, and we’ll monitor your heart and kidneys closely because of your other conditions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2132-12-21 14:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My heart’s been okay lately. But I know I have to be careful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2132-12-21 14:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we see you’re on several medications for heart failure, blood pressure, and diabetes. We’ll keep those managed carefully. For now, we’ll start IV fluids and keep you NPO—nothing by mouth—until after surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2132-12-21 14:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. When’s the surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2132-12-21 14:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Later this afternoon. The team is prepping the OR now. I’ll come back before we take you down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2132-12-21 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. You’re back from surgery. Everything went well—debridement and graft were successful. The VAC is in place at 75 mmHg. You’re doing great."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2132-12-21 16:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Is the graft sticking?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2132-12-21 16:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s too early to say for sure, but it looks good so far. We’ll keep you on bed rest for a few days to protect it. We’ve also placed a Foley catheter to help with mobility issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2132-12-21 16:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I figured. It’s hard to get up with my size and breathing issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2132-12-21 16:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring your oxygen closely. You’re on 3 liters, and your lungs sound clear. We also checked a chest X-ray to confirm your PICC line is still in place—it is."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2132-12-21 16:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I don’t want any infections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2132-12-21 16:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve stopped the antibiotics since it was just for prevention. Your labs look stable—creatinine is 1.3, which is normal for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2132-12-22 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. How’s the pain today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2132-12-22 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Manageable. I took the acetaminophen they gave me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2132-12-22 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll keep that going. You can start sipping water and we’ll advance to a light diet if you tolerate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2132-12-22 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I have some juice? I’m really thirsty."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2132-12-22 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Let’s start with small sips of water. If no nausea, we’ll try juice later. Your diabetes meds are on hold for now—we’re watching your glucose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2132-12-23 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor, I had some chest tightness last night. Left side. It’s gone now, but I was scared."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2132-12-23 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I saw the note. We did an EKG and checked troponin and CK-MB. Everything was normal, and your EKG looks the same as before surgery. It was likely musculoskeletal, but we’re keeping an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2132-12-23 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. My heart’s always a worry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2132-12-23 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We know. That’s why we’re being cautious. Your urine output is good—over 50 cc per hour—so your kidneys are handling things well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2132-12-24 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine went up a little—to 1.6 today. But your urine output is still strong, so we don’t think it’s acute kidney injury. We’re not giving a fluid bolus because of your heart history, but we’re watching closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2132-12-24 08:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that bad? My last admission was for kidney issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2132-12-24 08:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a small rise, and given your history, we’re cautious. But no signs of overload or dehydration. It may just be a blip. We’ll recheck tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2132-12-25 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your creatinine is back down to 1.1. Looks like it was temporary. Your graft site is also looking stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2132-12-25 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Can I start moving a bit?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2132-12-25 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. Still bed rest. But we’ll reassess in a day or two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2132-12-26 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today we’ll remove the VAC to check the graft. If it’s holding, we can start getting you up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2132-12-26 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m nervous. What if it didn’t take?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2132-12-26 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll know soon. But your wound looked well-vascularized in the last exam, which is a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2132-12-26 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great news—the graft is intact and healthy. No signs of necrosis. We’re discontinuing the VAC and removing the Foley."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2132-12-26 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, thank goodness. I can finally get up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2132-12-26 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, activity as tolerated. Physical therapy will come by to help you walk safely. We’ll also restart your glargine insulin at 12 units tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2132-12-26 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve missed moving around."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2132-12-27 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well with PT yesterday. Your leg is stable, and you’re healing well. We’re planning to discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2132-12-27 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "To the rehab center again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2132-12-27 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, extended care. You’ll continue wound care there, and we’ll see you in two weeks to remove staples."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2132-12-27 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What meds will I be on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2132-12-27 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most of your usual ones—lisinopril, metoprolol, furosemide, simvastatin, pantoprazole, and glargine. Plus aspirin daily and heparin shots for blood clots."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2132-12-27 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And pain medicine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2132-12-27 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Acetaminophen and oxycodone for breakthrough pain. But don’t drive while taking it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2132-12-27 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Any restrictions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2132-12-27 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep the leg elevated, avoid standing too long. You can shower—just cover the graft with a Tegaderm and don’t scrub it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2132-12-27 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And when do I call the doctor?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2132-12-27 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you have fever over 100.5, increased redness, sudden pain, or drainage from the graft. Also, weigh yourself daily—call if you gain more than 3 pounds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2132-12-27 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that. Thanks for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Final check before discharge. You’re afebrile, pain is controlled, and your graft looks excellent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel ready. Nervous, but ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done great. Keep up with your care, eat well, and follow up in two weeks. You’re on the right track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I really appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing—should I keep using the CPAP?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, especially with your obesity hypoventilation and sleep apnea. It helps your breathing and heart. We know you’ve had trouble before, but please try to use it nightly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do my best. I know it’s important."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s all we ask. Keep working on it. Your health depends on these small steps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Just keep following the plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I want to get better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And you are. This graft is a big step forward."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad I came back for it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "So are we. It gives your wound the best chance to heal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll take care of it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the spirit. We’ll see you in clinic soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Looking forward to it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take it easy, and call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Alright, the transport team will get you ready to go."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. Get some rest and keep healing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Bye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2132-12-28 10:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Goodbye."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2132-12-21 14:00:00",
    "admission_end": "2132-12-28 18:48:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with multiple comorbidities, including morbid obesity, diabetes, congestive heart failure, atrial fibrillation, and obstructive sleep apnea, was admitted for a planned split-thickness skin graft to treat a non-healing right lower extremity wound sustained two weeks prior. She underwent successful debridement and grafting, with a wound vacuum placed postoperatively. Her recovery was complicated by a transient rise in creatinine to 1.6 on postoperative day 3, which resolved spontaneously without intervention, and a brief episode of left-sided chest pain that was ruled out for cardiac ischemia. The graft remained intact, and she was mobilized on postoperative day 6. She was discharged to extended care with instructions for wound care, activity progression, and follow-up in two weeks for staple removal. At discharge, she was afebrile, hemodynamically stable, and in good condition.",
    "problems": [
      "Open wound of knee, leg [except thigh], and ankle, complicated",
      "Obesity hypoventilation syndrome",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified",
      "Chronic diastolic heart failure",
      "Atrial fibrillation",
      "Chronic airway obstruction, not elsewhere classified",
      "Migraine, unspecified, without mention of intractable migraine without mention of status migrainosus",
      "Body Mass Index 50.0-59.9, adult",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Unspecified accident",
      "Accidents occurring in unspecified place",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of native coronary artery",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult)(pediatric)",
      "Personal history of noncompliance with medical treatment, presenting hazards to health",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Other and unspecified alcohol dependence, in remission",
      "Cocaine abuse, in remission",
      "Other premature beats",
      "Long-term (current) use of aspirin",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Need for prophylactic vaccination and inoculation against influenza",
      "Venous (peripheral) insufficiency, unspecified",
      "Morbid obesity"
    ]
  }
}
